{# ===========================================================================
   Component: the Hours row of the NAP plate.

   One implementation for all three location templates. The row used to be
   written out separately in each, which is how Convoy ended up with no Hours
   row at all while the other two carried "Being confirmed. Call the room."

   Expects `loc` in scope.

   Hours confirmed 2026-09-09 by Connor for six of seven. Maui was not
   supplied, so it keeps the honest fallback rather than borrowing a sibling's
   pattern: CLIENT_FACTS.md's rule is do not publish hours the door does not
   honor, and that has not changed for Maui.

   Days come from the `dayRange` filter, times straight from locations.json.
   The same array feeds openingHoursSpecification in _data/schema.js, so the
   visible row and the graph cannot drift.
   =========================================================================== #}
<span class="plate__item">
  <span class="plate__label">Hours</span>
  {%- if loc.hours and loc.hours.length %}
  <span class="plate__value plate__value--hours">
    {%- for rule in loc.hours %}
    <span class="plate__hours-row">
      <span class="plate__hours-days">{{ rule.days | dayRange }}</span>
      <span class="plate__hours-time">{{ rule.opens }} to {{ rule.closes }}</span>
    </span>
    {%- endfor %}
  </span>
  {%- else %}
  <span class="plate__value">Call the room</span>
  {%- endif %}
</span>
